Z||000003||bHooper||06-02-2000||02:53 PM||||Tal, I gotta do the same thing this weekend.  Never got mine tight enough and it chattered its way into oblivion.<P>Anyone have a tip on tightening a belt?  I have never done this before.  <P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||06-02-2000||03:10 PM||||Tal & Hoop, The easiest way i have found to do this is to use a large screwdriver/prybar/tire-iron whatever to hold the alt while feeling the tension on the belt. A properly tightened belt will have approx. 1/4" to 1/2" of play (up + down movement). Once this is acheived use the prementioned tool to hold the alt and tighten down the bolts. Recheck movement after tightening. ||||reg||1
